.TH OPENROUTER 1 "2026-09-08" "openrouter" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openrouter \- track OpenRouter model prices and benchmark scores in a local table, TUI, and generated document
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openrouter
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ flags ]
.PP
.B openrouter
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.PP
.B openrouter
.RB { \-v | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B openrouter
collects prices and context length from the public OpenRouter API, and quality
scores from swebench.com, vals.ai and arena.ai, joined through the manual
.I model\-map.tsv
mapping, then regenerates a markdown comparison document. Prose annotations
live in
.IR notes.yaml ;
edits made directly to the generated
.I .md
file are overwritten on the next
.B refresh
run.
.PP
Besides the markdown document,
.B openrouter
offers two local views of the same data: a plain\-text
.B table
for scripting and piping, and an interactive
.B tui
for browsing, sorting, filtering, and inspecting individual models.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B refresh
Fetch fresh data from the network and overwrite the generated document and
local snapshot. Aliases:
.BR update ", " up .
.TP
.B check
Report only: new candidate models, removed slugs, and
.I notes.yaml
gaps against the local snapshot recorded by the last successful
.BR refresh .
Writes nothing. (Not to be confused with the unrelated Makefile
.B check
target, which is a dependency-freshness gate for maintainers, not this
command; the Makefile equivalent of this command is
.BR "make cli-check" .)
.TP
.B table
Show local model data as a plain\-text table, using the most recent local
snapshot (from the last
.B refresh
or
.BR check ).
.TP
.B tui
Browse local model data in an interactive terminal table. See
.B HOTKEYS
below.
.TP
.B history
Show price history recorded by past
.B refresh
runs.
.TP
.B init
Create a user config file and the local cache directory.
.TP
.B version
Print the binary version and exit successfully.
.TP
.B completion
Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
.RB ( bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", or " powershell ).
.TP
.B bash_completion
Print the Bash completion script directly, without going through
.BR "completion bash" ;
both generate the identical script from the same command tree.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit successfully.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIstring\fR
Path to
.IR config.yaml .
Default:
.IR $HOME/.config/openrouter/config.yaml .
.TP
.B \-\-data\-dir \fIstring\fR
Project directory containing
.IR model\-map.tsv ", " notes.yaml ", and " cache/ .
Overrides the value in the config file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Help for
.B openrouter
or the current subcommand; always prints the running version as its first
line, before any other help content.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit successfully.
.PP
Each subcommand accepts its own additional flags; run
.B "openrouter <command> --help"
for the full list. The most commonly used are:
.TP
.B \-\-output \fIstring\fR
.RB ( refresh ", " check )
Path to the generated markdown document; overrides the config value.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
.RB ( refresh )
Write nothing: neither the document nor the local snapshot.
.TP
.B \-\-model \fIstring\fR ", " \-\-since \fIstring\fR ", " \-\-format \fIstring\fR
.RB ( history )
Filter by slug, show observations after an RFC3339 timestamp or
.IR YYYY\-MM\-DD ,
and choose
.B markdown
(default) or
.B tsv
output.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sort " \fIstring\fR"
.RB ( table ", " tui )
Sort by
.BR name ", " slug ", " context ", " input ", " output ", " price ", " quality " (Q), " q/p " (QP), or " utility ", " P .
Default:
.IR utility .
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-reverse
.RB ( table ", " tui )
Reverse the primary sort order.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filter " \fIstring\fR"
.RB ( table ", " tui )
Structured, comma\-separated filter predicates (repeatable on
.BR table );
see the TUI's own
.B f
filter editor and its help text for the full predicate grammar.
.TP
.B \-\-ranking \fIstring\fR
.RB ( table ", " tui )
Ranking mode:
.BR legacy " (q/p); " tier " or " tier\-priority "; " mixed " or " mixed\-utility .
Default:
.IR mixed\-utility .
.TP
.B \-\-score\-source \fIstring\fR
.RB ( table ", " tui )
Score source for status and ranking:
.BR swebench " (SWE\-bench Verified) or " arena " (LMArena Elo); the two are never mixed."
Default:
.IR swebench .
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-interval \fIduration\fR
.RB ( tui )
Automatic live refresh interval; 0 disables it (the
.B R
hotkey always refreshes on demand). Default:
.IR 5m0s .
.SH HOTKEYS
The interactive
.B tui
is driven by many context-specific hotkeys (main list, Settings, model
detail, columns, filter, and help itself). This section mirrors the TUI's
own help overlay
.RB ( ? " or " F1 ,
Hotkeys section; six sections total: Overview, Score Sources, Hotkeys,
Filters, Model Detail, Methodology; see also
.IR docs/reference.md )
exactly: category names, their order, and the ordered key list within each
category are the same on both surfaces, and an automated test
(TestHotkeyConsistency, cmd/openrouter/hotkey_consistency_test.go) fails the
build if they ever drift apart. Each entry below describes exactly one
action; where two or more keys are listed together, they are equivalent
ways to trigger that same one action.
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B Up
(Settings) Previous Settings field.
.TP
.B Down
(Settings) Next Settings field.
.TP
.B Esc
(Settings) Close Settings.
.TP
.B Up
(Model detail) Previous detail field.
.TP
.B Down
(Model detail) Next detail field.
.TP
.B Up
(Help) Scroll help up.
.TP
.B Down
(Help) Scroll help down.
.TP
.B Up
(Columns) Previous column.
.TP
.B Down
(Columns) Next column.
.TP
.B Esc
(Columns) Cancel column selection.
.TP
.B Up
(Filter) Previous filter field.
.TP
.B Down
(Filter) Next filter field.
.TP
.B Esc
(Filter) Cancel filter editing.
.TP
.B Up
(Main list) Previous model; in help, scroll up.
.TP
.B Down
(Main list) Next model; in help, scroll down.
.TP
.BR j " / " k
Move through models; in help, scroll.
.TP
.BR Home " / " g
Jump to the first item.
.TP
.BR End " / " G
Jump to the last item.
.TP
.BR PgUp " / " PgDown
Page through models or help.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Right
Open the selected model's detail screen.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " Left ", or " h
Close the current screen and return to the list.
.SS Data/view
.TP
.B q
Sort by quality.
.TP
.B p
Cycle availability: any, free, paid, any.
.TP
.B r
Sort by quality-per-price ratio (Q/P).
.TP
.B v
Toggle layout: all models vs top-paid-free.
.TP
.B l
Toggle the UI language: English vs Russian; works from any screen.
.TP
.B m
Toggle ranking mode: mixed-utility vs tier-priority.
.TP
.B s
Cycle the sort key.
.TP
.B S
Reverse the sort order.
.TP
.B o
Open Settings (ranking, score source, filter, columns).
.TP
.B Down
(Settings) Move to Score source.
.TP
.B Space
(Main list) Switch score source: SWE\-bench vs Arena.
.TP
.B Space
(Settings) Switch score source: SWE\-bench vs Arena.
.TP
.B R
Refresh local data.
.TP
.B c
Open column selection.
.TP
.B n
Switch the last column between Task fit and Note.
.SS Filters/settings
.TP
.B f
Edit the structured filter.
.TP
.B /
Search Name/Slug.
.TP
.B Space
(Columns) Toggle a column.
.TP
.B Enter
(Columns) Apply the column selection.
.TP
.B Space
(Filter) Cycle Tier.
.TP
.B Enter
Apply the current editor.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel the current editor.
.SS Task-fit codes
.TP
.B I
implement: write or change production code.
.TP
.B P
plan: define scope, steps, and decisions.
.TP
.B R
research: investigate options, evidence, or behavior.
.TP
.B D
debug: find and fix a defect or failure.
.TP
.B A
audit: inspect quality, safety, or compliance.
.TP
.B F
refactor: improve structure without changing behavior.
.TP
.B T
test: add or improve automated verification.
.PP
No task-fit classification is shown as n/a.
.SS "Refresh and finish"
.TP
.B R
Refresh local data now. Auto-refresh uses
.BR \-\-refresh\-interval ;
.B 0
disables it.
.TP
.B "mouse drag"
Select any visible text;
.B y
copies the selection again.
.TP
.BR x " / " Ctrl\-C
Exit the TUI.
.TP
.B Esc
Close help.
.TP
.B Esc
Return to the list from the current overlay.
.TP
.B ?
Close help.
.TP
.B F1
Open full help.
.SS "Help search"
.TP
.B /
Start a search in this document; type text and press Enter.
.TP
.B n
Go to the next match; search results stay selected.
.TP
.B N
Go to the previous match; search results stay selected.
.TP
.BR Up " / " Down
Scroll this help; they do not change the selected match.
.TP
.B "0 matches"
Searches with no matches are reported explicitly.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel search.
.SS General/help
.TP
.B Esc
Close the main view.
.TP
.BR x " / " Ctrl\-C
Exit the TUI.
.TP
.B ?
Open help at the Hotkeys section.
.TP
.B ?
Close help.
.TP
.B F1
Open full help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Refresh local data and regenerate the document:
.RS
\fBopenrouter refresh\fR
.RE
.TP
Show the top 10 models by utility as a plain\-text table:
.RS
\fBopenrouter table \-\-limit 10\fR
.RE
.TP
Filter to paid models with quality at or above 80, sorted by price:
.RS
\fBopenrouter table \-\-filter 'paid,quality>=80' \-\-sort price\fR
.RE
.TP
Browse the data interactively, ranked by LMArena Elo:
.RS
\fBopenrouter tui \-\-score\-source arena\fR
.RE
.TP
Show price history for one model as TSV:
.RS
\fBopenrouter history \-\-model openai/gpt\-5.6\-luna \-\-format tsv\fR
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B openrouter
guarantees only two outcomes, not a documented set of distinct non-zero
codes:
.TP
.B 0
Success, including
.BR \-\-help / \-h / help .
.TP
.I non\-zero
Any failure: usage error (unknown command or flag, invalid argument value),
network or data error, or a write failure. This is a deliberate choice
(README.md, "Exit codes"), not an omission: distinct exit codes per failure
class are not part of this CLI's contract.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/openrouter/config.yaml
The user config file, created by
.BR "openrouter init" .
Never overwritten automatically after that; edit it directly to change the
data directory, default output path, TUI keymap, icons, or cache settings.
Owner-only permissions (mode 0600 file, 0700 directory).
.TP
.I <data\-dir>/model\-map.tsv
Manual mapping from OpenRouter slug to display tier and benchmark\-source
identifiers. Hand\-maintained.
.TP
.I <data\-dir>/notes.yaml
Prose annotations (display name, free\-text note, task\-fit classification)
merged into the generated document and the TUI. Hand\-maintained.
.TP
.I <data\-dir>/model\-snapshot.json
The local snapshot of the most recent successful
.B refresh
or
.BR check ,
read by
.BR table " and " tui
so they work offline between refreshes. Local application state, not
distributed with the tool; owner-only permissions.
.TP
.I <data\-dir>/cache/price\-history.json
Price history recorded on every
.B refresh
that has usable price data; read by
.BR history .
Owner-only permissions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to resolve the default config path
.RI ( $HOME/.config/openrouter/config.yaml )
via the standard user\-home\-directory lookup. Not read by any other part of
.BR openrouter .
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Fallback terminal width for
.B table
output when the terminal size cannot be queried directly (e.g. when stdout
is not a TTY). If unset or invalid, a built\-in default width is used
instead.
.PP
.B table
opens
.B less \-S
directly for paged output in a TTY (disable with
.BR \-\-no\-pager );
this is not driven by
.BR $PAGER .
Color output follows the terminal's own capabilities as detected by the
underlying terminal library; it is not configured through a dedicated
environment variable by this CLI.
.SH VERSION
The version reported by
.BR "openrouter version" " and " "openrouter --version"
comes from the running binary's own build metadata (embedded at build time
via
.BR "-ldflags -X main.version=..." ),
never from this man page; this page's own
.B .TH
date is updated independently and is not a source of truth for what a given
installed binary reports.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1)
